{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1018170-house-spirit","id":1018170,"title":"House spirit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-16T12:17:45-08:00","id":1018170,"title":"House spirit","content":"How would I go able erecting a protective spirit to protect a living place? Would I need a ritual or would I need to summon and bind it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T14:41:03-08:00","id":1018229,"title":"","content":"Spirit 2 to communicate with the spirit you wish to bargain with. Since you want him to protect your interests you should do it this way and jeep every thing mutually beneficial. Spirit 4 and you can force him to do it but it will probably pervert every thing you make it do. Much less helpful in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T15:16:57-08:00","id":1018234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1018170-house-spirit?p=1018229#post1018229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit 2 to communicate with the spirit you wish to bargain with. Since you want him to protect your interests you should do it this way and jeep every thing mutually beneficial. Spirit 4 and you can force him to do it but it will probably pervert every thing you make it do. Much less helpful in the long run.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would I ensure he's materalized in the house? Would he always be in the house 24/7 or would I have to call him in from the umbra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T17:03:29-08:00","id":1018264,"title":"","content":"If he agrees to protect it he would be there doing so as he is able. When a spirit makes a deal they stick to their side as long as the other party does their part they agreed to. <br /> <br /> He will only materialize if he needs to and most spirits can attack an enemy just fine without doing so, which is way better for the spirit since most of its aggressors will be unable to harm them unless they have attacks or powers that can cross the gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T17:15:59-08:00","id":1018269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1018170-house-spirit?p=1018264#post1018264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he agrees to protect it he would be there doing so as he is able. When a spirit makes a deal they stick to their side as long as the other party does their part they agreed to.<br /> <br /> He will only materialize if he needs to and most spirits can attack an enemy just fine without doing so, which is way better for the spirit since most of its aggressors will be unable to harm them unless they have attacks or powers that can cross the gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>They need materalize to manifest in the overworld and actually attack, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T17:26:19-08:00","id":1018272,"title":"","content":"Most spirits can use their charms without materialising.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T22:17:46-08:00","id":1018344,"title":"","content":"A spirit will need to Materialize to do direct physical actions like a simple physical attack.<br /> <br /> But if what you want is a physical guard, you're better off with dogs and hired thugs.<br /> <br /> The major benefit of using a spirit is to rely on things only a spirit can do.<br /> <br /> Spirits do what they do, so you have to seek and choose.<br /> <br /> You can have both, by the way. Spirit and dog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T23:23:48-08:00","id":1018358,"title":"","content":"You can also use Spirit 3 to awaken the spirit of the house itself, like you would any object. The house spirit won't be too terribly powerful on its own - especially not if it's a relatively new house with a weak presence in the world - but it can do a number of minor things. Watch and report any activity within its confines, alert you to rodent infestations or structural problems (like mold or dangerous cracks), foil break-ins with &quot;coincidental&quot; action (windows or doors that slam against people attempting to gain access, trip them with billowing curtains, creak and groan in an attempt to fool them into thinking someone is home, wake the sleeping owner in the event of intruders, even collapse sections of the ceiling strategically), and perhaps even repel foreign spirits from the home. So long as the owner treats the house well, keeps it in good repair, and gives thanks for a job well done, the house spirit will be a loyal ally. A house spirit that has served the owner (or their family) long enough may even burn itself to the ground, if it protects them and destroys their enemies.<br /> <br /> While making a pact with another spirit is still good for more specialized guarding capabilities, the house itself can be an invaluable ally once roused from slumber. Mages from ancient Rome to Japan understood the value of keeping a shrine devoted to the god of their house, and for good reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 12-17-2016, 02:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T20:14:04-08:00","id":1019582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1018170-house-spirit?p=1018358#post1018358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can also use Spirit 3 to awaken the spirit of the house itself, like you would any object. The house spirit won't be too terribly powerful on its own - especially not if it's a relatively new house with a weak presence in the world - but it can do a number of minor things. Watch and report any activity within its confines, alert you to rodent infestations or structural problems (like mold or dangerous cracks), foil break-ins with &quot;coincidental&quot; action (windows or doors that slam against people attempting to gain access, trip them with billowing curtains, creak and groan in an attempt to fool them into thinking someone is home, wake the sleeping owner in the event of intruders, even collapse sections of the ceiling strategically), and perhaps even repel foreign spirits from the home. So long as the owner treats the house well, keeps it in good repair, and gives thanks for a job well done, the house spirit will be a loyal ally. A house spirit that has served the owner (or their family) long enough may even burn itself to the ground, if it protects them and destroys their enemies.<br /> <br /> While making a pact with another spirit is still good for more specialized guarding capabilities, the house itself can be an invaluable ally once roused from slumber. Mages from ancient Rome to Japan understood the value of keeping a shrine devoted to the god of their house, and for good reason.</div> </div> </div> </div> Let's say I have a rock elemental guard my house, would the rock elemental be there 24/7, or would I have to summon him through traditional methods when an intruder comes into the house?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T22:22:57-08:00","id":1019616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1018170-house-spirit?p=1019582#post1019582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's say I have a rock elemental guard my house, would the rock elemental be there 24/7, or would I have to summon him through traditional methods when an intruder comes into the house?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you and the rock elemental agreed for it to stick around your house 24/7, then yes. Making a pact with a spirit is kind of like hiring a contractor, or in this case a security guard. Does the rock elemental want to be there all the time? Or are there other things it could or needs to do? That's up to the Storyteller. If it has interests outside your home, you need to make it worth the spirit's while. You'd also need to make the place itself comfortable for the spirit to reside it. Rock gardens and stone walls would probably be necessary for an earth elemental.<br /> <br /> If you had Time 4 and Entropy 3, you could combine it with the summoning spell to create one that &quot;hangs&quot; until a particular situation occurs. Like, for instance, an intruder. At which point the spirit will be summoned from wherever it happens to be. It will make its way as quickly as it can/desires to, though what it'll do when it gets there is a different matter. Spirit 2 can't force it to do anything. So if you do set this up, it would help to make a pact with the spirit ahead of time, so it agrees to come when called and do its duties as a guard. If you just summon a random rock elemental to your house, it's just as likely to kick your ass itself as help you with your burglar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}